    why: >
      INVARIANT — peers are the store; doorways project with peer-fallback (race_fetch).
      Code writing "App not found" or "App ZIP not available" is on the EPR/blob
      resolution path. Any NotFound arm MUST include: (a) a peer-fallback call
      (blob_fetch::race_fetch — wired via get_blob_or_heal/T17 behind GET /blob and the
      /apps resolver; keep NEW NotFound arms on that shared sequence),
      OR (b) an EPR-head-aware syncing-status body instead of a bare 404.
      Root cause and fix plan (read before adding a new resolution-path NotFound arm):
