  - id: heal-fills-never-moves
    class: inject
    when: { write: "*.rs", contains-any: ["stamp_declared_head", "StampMode", "projection_reconcile", "GapFill"] }
    validator: epr:validator-heal-fills-never-moves
    why: >
      INVARIANT — heal FILLS absence, it never MOVES authority. A projection-reconcile / stamp
      path uses `StampMode::{Declare, GapFill}`: `Declare` is ONLY for a canonical answer (the
      zome returns `canonical: bool`); a fallback resolve (`canonical == false`, e.g. a cold
      conductor's root-author election while the canonical link is not yet retrievable) MUST stamp
      `GapFill` — it may fill an empty row but must NEVER displace a declared/adopted row. Stamping
      a fallback over an adopted canonical converts every restart into a rollback (the 2026-07-11
      resurrection class: HEALED anchor restamped the OLD head 2 min after cross-conductor adoption,
      across 2,838 divergence-queued rows). Do not widen `Declare`, and do not key the guard on
      *who* writes (that froze forward adoption, defect #3) — key it on the authority the write
      CARRIES (`canonical`).
